{"type":"message","id":"1df10e3c","parentId":"8446bc0b","timestamp":"2026-03-21T19:13:01.107Z","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"**Analyzing skill usage**\n\nI’m thinking we need to follow the heartbeat and scan for skills before replying. I wonder if only one clearly applies? The guideline suggests using \"using-superpowers\" to establish how to find and use those skills, so is it mandatory? According to the developer, if there’s exactly one applicable skill, then I should use it. Right now, it seems like \"using-superpowers\" is the only relevant one, so maybe I should review that skill. Let's explore it!","thinkingSignature":"{\"id\":\"rs_0cc6e6dbdd8474000169beedb89b448191be178f8679f823ad\",\"type\":\"reasoning\",\"encrypted_content\":\"gAAAAABpvu29g4McqEk6SjpxSsU4e9DEWDczEfML9F88ZgxE-Y3pZk4KdgwC-DP2NFGMQC5-wL2h2rdF0FGtuGPEufbe9-ysj5LE0OSLptDpQ3XbguFEFrnrFbBJJpYvPiX3K7yPA81ZCHaVzoS7XzmCuP_f9Oq0CD97VF8Vm2SkeHeeYLlrmxwSnRRaokM0eIjB8Gup8mqN1WypemDjGMgE1xnunoL_SZrDP0QoHEz7JGXalzaVCS1UEylOPVpOBM7N57h3jvouUIYjE6CsbA_-cf_Fpv53XKIGbrvckfmwQlVEj_kISQ-gkzFQqpeSKlOoTkGG2DgHt7L3ByjOMu17VbbRDdgGPN-3iVki2oRxLNiF6JB3pwSrMrHOFJhzPugCB_jTj_x3BTTg_fmUR1kUbbbynSgffkVcLG2Yk3YxduLzDEahjQoCaUZfcJqBlC-1uQAZaXpq1Aq_QkxxxtIKa936KQn_UCCS9_V4ogbi6hCqvYXmJptWbEWjDMYT64m3f-SKokwmdPD-RKg1tpJBmu3DoNVLpdvssDOnk-rdvzWZHTiqMAqnXiTFn1zeHT78ISgrOGAsk9-2X5a5K8UMLy5qP6Wm3amLCS7z8ob8TGvW9ZsLu_qAVL5-895mAvu2zkVcTogT3maw57fC2hxw_IVNxwSf0cX2DDEMKs69YkIs8FzzEBj5B11KNIfzhS0Zg1GLFP5dSKIkdGOJSnCXKOQiJCFWFlPvXugMI8siy09tgYJ3RKT8nq7hYobl-p3PLg7VKtqSQezmctk_szTiV-wvNMJD2t_1ovL9iB3YbEcTQs2oBDhcpq6B0Hj-xPq54j-JdSdQOHz6_3M_19e-qVkCw7pzMlVOGyQBwifL2JcbflpyAAOgibkx2fOhXbWo2pvaAYeya0a0splkm201ZydphrjlZCP_uCK9xvR_zPMTpb-Z7-LL8UoBjImtjbOwb6E-tAKHc20S3A13liukz5SPxEZBe3-xlg6gs4lqQH_UDYnfTr7uxWKqGNkkWf0QgC2wbMr1XyaY_t_ALXnZ2KxYRyCjFcoAuknV5mxU0gD4D0_5s0dDw9VArhpCduwdibcOCAbd7VFbM8nW-8wCitcEoF3fVXSbrDK0BMtCgSnnrfvT9cocjfb4bd0_yRzoieri5_k9svLQimzus1mw2wUCmTIROKJlhvm_UjJV6oXIsqJSSvfvvnmMuhPf5Ix9fZELK-0kdmGDWIyMpwx-45x_X3UaqkyoZrGDWc7lXpOrH1T87nLzEfz1Es_BA3-5Pr3scr4fLShDhzGgnpQaOMFblWfs56qEWINSlP1a2ZikGTw0eFbYwSjGs_KKvqmiSrQZSa-0DTKi-bG6D0D899jHtNIL7OVb0dvc_7_I58_jOpK4WPJWu4zt898vO_JljmgaVH5-\",\"summary\":[{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Analyzing skill usage**\\n\\nI’m thinking we need to follow the heartbeat and scan for skills before replying. I wonder if only one clearly applies? The guideline suggests using \\\"using-superpowers\\\" to establish how to find and use those skills, so is it mandatory? According to the developer, if there’s exactly one applicable skill, then I should use it. Right now, it seems like \\\"using-superpowers\\\" is the only relevant one, so maybe I should review that skill. Let's explore it!\"}]}"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_lTmHSOAcpusVBhqopQ7kwzQc|fc_0cc6e6dbdd8474000169beedbcffdc81919df2e9c92990f9f1","name":"read","arguments":{"file_path":"/home/lfant/.agents/skills/using-superpowers/SKILL.md"},"partialJson":"{\"file_path\":\"/home/lfant/.agents/skills/using-superpowers/SKILL.md\"}"}],"api":"openai-codex-responses","provider":"openai-codex","model":"gpt-5.4","usage":{"input":19406,"output":117,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":19523,"cost":{"input":0.048515,"output":0.001755,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0.05027}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1774120373406}}
{"type":"message","id":"ee98b6b0","parentId":"1df10e3c","timestamp":"2026-03-21T19:13:01.115Z","message":{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_lTmHSOAcpusVBhqopQ7kwzQc|fc_0cc6e6dbdd8474000169beedbcffdc81919df2e9c92990f9f1","toolName":"read","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\nname: using-superpowers\ndescription: Use when starting any conversation - establishes how to find and use skills, requiring Skill tool invocation before ANY response including clarifying questions\n---\n\n<EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\nIf you think there is even a 1% chance a skill might apply to what you are doing, you ABSOLUTELY MUST invoke the skill.\n\nIF A SKILL APPLIES TO YOUR TASK, YOU DO NOT HAVE A CHOICE. YOU MUST USE IT.\n\nThis is not negotiable. This is not optional. You cannot rationalize your way out of this.\n</EXTREMELY-IMPORTANT>\n\n## How to Access Skills\n\n**In Claude Code:** Use the `Skill` tool. When you invoke a skill, its content is loaded and presented to you—follow it directly. Never use the Read tool on skill files.\n\n**In other environments:** Check your platform's documentation for how skills are loaded.\n\n# Using Skills\n\n## The Rule\n\n**Invoke relevant or requested skills BEFORE any response or action.** Even a 1% chance a skill might apply means that you should invoke the skill to check. If an invoked skill turns out to be wrong for the situation, you don't need to use it.\n\n```dot\ndigraph skill_flow {\n    \"User message received\" [shape=doublecircle];\n    \"About to EnterPlanMode?\" [shape=doublecircle];\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" [shape=box];\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Invoke Skill tool\" [shape=box];\n    \"Announce: 'Using [skill] to [purpose]'\" [shape=box];\n    \"Has checklist?\" [shape=diamond];\n    \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" [shape=box];\n    \"Follow skill exactly\" [shape=box];\n    \"Respond (including clarifications)\" [shape=doublecircle];\n\n    \"About to EnterPlanMode?\" -> \"Already brainstormed?\";\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" -> \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Already brainstormed?\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Invoke brainstorming skill\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\";\n\n    \"User message received\" -> \"Might any skill apply?\";\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" -> \"Invoke Skill tool\" [label=\"yes, even 1%\"];\n    \"Might any skill apply?\" -> \"Respond (including clarifications)\" [label=\"definitely not\"];\n    \"Invoke Skill tool\" -> \"Announce: 'Using [skill] to [purpose]'\";\n    \"Announce: 'Using [skill] to [purpose]'\" -> \"Has checklist?\";\n    \"Has checklist?\" -> \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" [label=\"yes\"];\n    \"Has checklist?\" -> \"Follow skill exactly\" [label=\"no\"];\n    \"Create TodoWrite todo per item\" -> \"Follow skill exactly\";\n}\n```\n\n## Red Flags\n\nThese thoughts mean STOP—you're rationalizing:\n\n| Thought | Reality |\n|---------|---------|\n| \"This is just a simple question\" | Questions are tasks. Check for skills. |\n| \"I need more context first\" | Skill check comes BEFORE clarifying questions. |\n| \"Let me explore the codebase first\" | Skills tell you HOW to explore. Check first. |\n| \"I can check git/files quickly\" | Files lack conversation context. Check for skills. |\n| \"Let me gather information first\" | Skills tell you HOW to gather information. |\n| \"This doesn't need a formal skill\" | If a skill exists, use it. |\n| \"I remember this skill\" | Skills evolve. Read current version. |\n| \"This doesn't count as a task\" | Action = task. Check for skills. |\n| \"The skill is overkill\" | Simple things become complex. Use it. |\n| \"I'll just do this one thing first\" | Check BEFORE doing anything. |\n| \"This feels productive\" | Undisciplined action wastes time. Skills prevent this. |\n| \"I know what that means\" | Knowing the concept ≠ using the skill. Invoke it. |\n\n## Skill Priority\n\nWhen multiple skills could apply, use this order:\n\n1. **Process skills first** (brainstorming, debugging) - these determine HOW to approach the task\n2. **Implementation skills second** (frontend-design, mcp-builder) - these guide execution\n\n\"Let's build X\" → brainstorming first, then implementation skills.\n\"Fix this bug\" → debugging first, then domain-specific skills.\n\n## Skill Types\n\n**Rigid** (TDD, debugging): Follow exactly. Don't adapt away discipline.\n\n**Flexible** (patterns): Adapt principles to context.\n\nThe skill itself tells you which.\n\n## User Instructions\n\nInstructions say WHAT, not HOW. \"Add X\" or \"Fix Y\" doesn't mean skip workflows.\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1774120381113}}
